dd0d5c1091331","ma-c-0b7d0f6b7649746864a1","ma-c-0fade4f68d63871db566","ma-c-130c67863b637131aae4","ma-c-1acd6cefef58f7d3c8b6","ma-c-1e273a3431b03d87fea2","ma-c-24eae61d2dbed5aa613d","ma-c-3531a091aa40b6ad4035","ma-c-3641c06b342b2f041827","ma-c-4447c27bf7058aa4a6aa","ma-c-471958fdba4a2ec52cfc","ma-c-4d7caa47262c3cd60a0b","ma-c-524d7ca4bc9ffccbaa70","ma-c-5a499f9cd2303775c0a5","ma-c-5f4e6f08216f779c628c","ma-c-70c9fe2798cf9449bb8c","ma-c-95728ec67baa8c959b60","ma-c-9bc5250e78b9da2bfcb5","ma-c-ace903ce12c4d437658c","ma-c-ae84fb20208684921017","ma-c-b3aa148f9a481156f5cb","ma-c-b45bc318e0cb44df1356","ma-c-b5748562b2d66ce96d8f","ma-c-b9f15768d4df6fe18cf8","ma-c-bcd4071d5c4a9471d3ae","ma-c-c36f2659edf14446c5bf","ma-c-c5a688e541be0e41d67a","ma-c-d1f90e8e2f2f5cc5b146","ma-c-d55c064626e069884b44","ma-c-e11c243db48e98912c1a","ma-c-e4b5f5ef6af9fb649f0f","ma-c-e7b34cffae908ab556fc","ma-c-e824e0a3e8335f5f4f97","ma-c-eed24a96bfadc84a226b","ma-c-f5326d6d3eabad4763cc","ma-c-f86052cb7cfbcf3f68e0","ma-c-fc5467d7617b6f083cd3"],"papers":{"arXiv:2607.24334":{"abstract":"The evaluation homomorphism from the super Yangian \\( \\mathrm{Y}(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n}) \\) to \\( \\mathrm{U}(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n}) \\) induces a \\( \\mathrm{Y}(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n}) \\)-module structure on any finite dimensional simple \\( \\mathrm{U}(\\mathfrak{gl}_{m|n}) \\)-module \\( L(λ) \\). In this paper, we give necessary and sufficient conditions for the tensor product of such evaluation \\( \\mathrm{Y}(","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Zheng Li","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2026"},"arXiv:1409.0550":{"abstract":"The classical Gelfand-Tsetlin formulas provide a basis in terms of tableaux and an explicit action of the generators of $\\mathfrak{gl} (n)$ for every irreducible finite-dimensional $\\mathfrak{gl} (n)$-module. These formulas can be used to define a $\\mathfrak{gl} (n)$-module structure on some infinite-dimensional modules - the so-called generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules. The generic Gelfand-Tsetlin m","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2014"},"arXiv:1605.07580":{"abstract":"For an admissible affine vertex algebra $V_k(\\mathfrak{g})$ of type $A$, we describe a new family of relaxed highest weight representations of $V_k(\\mathfrak{g})$. They are simple quotients of representations of the affine Kac-Moody algebra $\\widehat{\\mathfrak{g}}$ induced from the following $\\mathfrak{g}$-modules: 1) generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules in the principal nilpotent orbit, in particular ","authors":["Tomoyuki Arakawa","Vyacheslav Futorny","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:0801.0903":{"abstract":"We address two problems regarding the structure and representation theory of finite W-algebras associated with the general linear Lie algebras. Finite W-algebras can be defined either via the Whittaker model of Kostant or, equivalently, by the quantum Hamiltonian reduction. Our first main result is a proof of the Gelfand-Kirillov conjecture for the skew fields of fractions of the finite W-algebras","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Alexander Molev","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2008"},"arXiv:1611.07908":{"abstract":"We propose a new effective method of constructing explicitly Gelfand -Tsetlin modules for $\\mathfrak{gl}_n$. We obtain a large family of simple modules that have a basis consisting of Gelfand-Tsetlin tableaux, the action of the Lie algebra is given by the Gelfand-Tsetlin formulas and with all Gelfand-Tsetlin multiplicities equal $1$. As an application of our construction we prove necessary and suf","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Luis Enrique Ramirez","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:1704.01209":{"abstract":"We prove a uniqueness theorem for irreducible non-critical Gelfand-Tsetlin modules. The uniqueness result leads to a complete classification of the irreducible Gelfand-Tsetlin modules with 1-singularity. An explicit construction of such modules was given in \\cite{FGR2}. In particular, we show that the modules constructed in \\cite{FGR2} exhaust all irreducible Gelfand-Tsetlin modules with 1-singula","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1409.8413":{"abstract":"We provide a classification and explicit bases of tableaux of all irreducible generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules for the Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{gl}(n)$.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2014"},"arXiv:2002.05568":{"abstract":"We explicitly construct, in terms of Gelfand--Tsetlin tableaux, a new family of simple positive energy representations for the simple affine vertex algebra V_k(sl_{n+1}) in the minimal nilpotent orbit of sl_{n+1}. These representations are quotients of induced modules over the affine Kac-Moody algebra of sl_n+1 and include in particular all admissible simple highest weight modules and all simple m","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Oscar Armando Hernandez Morales","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2020"},"arXiv:1812.07137":{"abstract":"We provide a classification and an explicit realization of all irreducible Gelfand-Tsetlin modules of the complex Lie algebra sl(3). The realization of these modules uses regular and derivative Gelfand-Tsetlin tableaux. In particular, we list all simple Gelfand-Tsetlin sl(3)-modules with infinite-dimensional weight spaces. Also, we express all simple Gelfand-Tsetlin sl(3)-modules as subquotionets ","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Dimitar Grantcharov","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:1610.08126":{"abstract":"We provide a classification and explicit bases of tableaux of all irreducible subquotients of generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules over Uq(gl(n)) where q different 1 and -1.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Enrique Ramirez","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:math/0610071":{"abstract":"We solve the problem of extension of characters of commutative subalgebras in associative (noncommutative) algebras for a class of subrings (Galois orders) in skew group rings. These results can be viewed as a noncommutative analogue of liftings of prime ideals in the case of integral extensions of commutative rings. The proposed approach can be applied to the representation theory of many infinit","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2006"},"arXiv:1712.03700":{"abstract":"In the present paper we describe a new class of Gelfand--Tsetlin modules for an arbitrary complex simple finite-dimensional Lie algebra g and give their geometric realization as the space of delta-functions\" on the flag manifold G/B supported at the 1-dimensional submanifold. When g=sl(n) (or gl(n)) these modules form a subclass of Gelfand-Tsetlin modules with infinite dimensional weight subspaces","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Libor Krizka"],"year":"2017"}}}